ne\",\"id\":\"$undefined\",\"className\":\"text-gray-900 font-bold leading-rem30px text-rem25px bp600:text-rem32px bp600:leading-rem38px print:text-rem19px print:leading-rem27px print:font-semibold mt-rem32px mb-rem16px break-words print:mt-rem12px print:text-rem19px print:leading-rem27px print:font-semibold print:mb-rem8px  \",\"children\":[\"What are head injury treatments?\"]}],[\"$\",\"p\",\"2709ca1a63e7\",{\"data-identity\":\"paragraph-element\",\"className\":\"text-gray-800 my-rem16px text-rem19px leading-rem34px print:text-rem15px print:leading-rem20px print:font-normal print:my-rem8px  \",\"children\":[\"Your provider will suggest treatments based on which type of head injury you have (and its severity). The most important part of treating any head injury is preventing bleeding and a buildup of pressure inside your skull. This will protect your brain and prevent complications.\"]}],[\"$\",\"p\",\"a471df6a73ad\",{\"data-identity\":\"paragraph-element\",\"className\":\"text-gray-800 my-rem16px text-rem19px leading-rem34px print:text-rem15px print:leading-rem20px print:font-normal print:my-rem8px  \",\"children\":[\"Most people with mild injuries can manage symptoms at home with rest and by avoiding intense physical activities. If it’s safe for you to take \",[\"$\",\"a\",\"91399753ede01\",{\"data-identity\":\"link\",\"href\":\"https://my.clevelandclinic.org/health/treatments/12058-pain-relievers\",\"target\":\"_blank\",\"className\":\"text-brandBlue-500 print:text-black underline underline-offset-[5px] print:no-underline decoration-1 break-words hover:text-blue-800 transition\",\"children\":[\"pain relievers\"]}],\", your provider will suggest over-the-counter (OTC) acetaminophen. Most people can’t take \",[\"$\",\"a\",\"91399753ede03\",{\"data-identity\":\"link\",\"href\":\"https://my.clevelandclinic.org/health/treatments/11086-non-steroidal-anti-inflammatory-medicines-nsaids\",\"target\":\"_blank\",\"className\":\"text-brandBlue-500 print:text-black underline underline-offset-[5px] print:no-underline decoration-1 break-words hover:text-blue-800 transition\",\"children\":[\"NSAIDs\"]}],\" after a head injury because they can increase the risk of bleeding inside your skull.\"]}],[\"$\",\"div\",\"a471df6a73ad_mobile_ad\",{\"data-identity\":\"billboard-ad\",\"className\":\"flex bp1100:hidden print:hidden max-w-[400px] min-w-[300px] m-auto items-center justify-center bg-gray-300 pt-rem16px pb-[3.125rem] my-rem32px  \",\"children\":[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"max-w-[300px] mx-auto\",\"children\":[null,[\"$\",\"p\",null,{\"className\":\"text-"])</script><script>self.__next_f.push([1,"gray-800 uppercase text-rem10px leading-rem16px mx-auto w-fit\",\"children\":\"Advertisement\"}],[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"flex bp1100:hidden flex-col items-center justify-center\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"data-identity\":\"ad-slot\",\"id\":\"billboard4_300x250_mobile\",\"className\":\"ad-reset w-[300px] !min-h-[250px] flex bg-gray-300\"}],null]}]]}]}],[\"$\",\"p\",\"d975fc594ae9\",{\"data-identity\":\"paragraph-element\",\"className\":\"text-gray-800 my-rem16px text-rem19px leading-rem34px print:text-rem15px print:leading-rem20px print:font-normal print:my-rem8px  \",\"children\":[\"If you have a specific injury like a concussion or skull fracture, your provider will tell you what to expect. They’ll give a customized treatment and recovery plan based on the specific injury you have.\"]}],\"$L80\",\"$L81\",\"$L82\",\"$L83\",\"$L84\",\"$L85\"]}]]}],\"$L86\"]}]\n57:[\"$\",\"div\",\"b8120abac7bfddd60eaf8c4bd07e11c7\",{\"children\":[[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"data-identity\":\"article-section\",\"id\":\"outlook-prognosis\",\"className\":\"scroll-mt-[112px]\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"h2\",null,{\"data-identity\":\"headline\",\"id\":\"$undefined\",\"className\":\"text-gray-900 font-bold leading-rem34px text-rem32px bp600:text-rem40px bp600:leading-rem44px print:text-rem22px print:leading-rem31px print:font-bold mt-rem56px print:mt-rem24px mb-rem16px print:mb-rem8px print:text-rem22px print:leading-rem31px print:font-bold break-words\",\"children\":\"Outlook / Prognosis\"}],\"$undefined\",[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"data-identity\":\"rich-text\",\"className\":\" after:content-[''] after:table\",\"id\":\"$undefined\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"h3\",\"6d82d8890845\",{\"data-identity\":\"headline\",\"id\":\"$undefined\",\"className\":\"text-gray-900 font-bold leading-rem30px text-rem25px bp600:text-rem32px bp600:leading-rem38px print:text-rem19px print:leading-rem27px print:font-semibold mt-rem32px mb-rem16px break-words print:mt-rem12px print:text-rem19px print:leading-rem27px print:font-semibold print:mb-rem8px  \",\"children\":[\"What can I expect if I have a head injury?\"]}],[\"$\",\"p\",\"1abce50741d6\",{\"data-identity\":\"paragraph-element\",\"className\":\"text-gray-800 my-rem16px text-rem19px leading-rem34px print:text-rem15px print:leading-rem20px print:font-normal print:my-rem8px  \",\"children\":[\"Everyone’s body responds to head injuries differently.\"]}],[\"$\",\"p\",\"d7c8592a03f4\",{\"data-identity\":\"paragraph-element\",\"className\":\"text-gray-800 my-rem16px text-rem19px leading-rem34px print:text-rem15px print:leading-rem20px print:font-normal print:my-rem8px  \",\"children\":[\"Some people take a few weeks to recover from an injury, but sometimes, head injuries can naturally take months (or longer) to heal.\"]}],[\"$\",\"p\",\"65b7eb8fcf0e\",{\"data-identity\":\"paragraph-element\",\"className\":\"text-gray-800 my-rem16px text-rem19px leading-rem34px print:text-rem15px print:leading-rem20px print:font-normal print:my-rem8px  \",\"children\":[\"Talk to your provider before resuming your usual daily routine. Don’t return to exercise, training or playing sports until your provider says it’s safe. Giving your body the time it needs to heal doesn’t mean you’re weak. And rushing your recovery to get back to practice, games, training or work doesn’t mean you’re extra tough.\"]}]]}]]}],false]}]\n58:[\"$\",\"div\",\"22dc21ea4d0e1c5c95091109af673b6a\",{\"children\":[[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"data-identity\":\"article-section\",\"id\":\"prevention\",\"className\":\"scroll-mt-[112px]\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"h2\",null,{\"data-identity\":\"headline\",\"id\":\"$undefined\",\"className\":\"text-gray-900 font-bold leading-rem34px text-rem32px bp600:text-rem40px bp600:leading-rem44px print:text-rem22px print:leading-rem31px print:font-bold mt-rem56px print:mt-rem24px mb-rem16px print:mb-rem8px print:text-rem22px print:leading-rem31px print:font-bold break-words\",\"children\":\"Prevention\"}],\"$undefined\",[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"data-identity\":\"rich-text\",\"className\":\" after:content-[''] after:table\",\"id\":\"$undefined\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"h3\",\"38c81f1480ef\",{\"data-identity\":\"headline\",\"id\":\"$undefined\",\"className\":\"text-gray-900 font-bold leading-rem30px text-rem25px bp600:text-rem32px bp600:leading-rem38px print:text-rem19px print:leading-rem27px print:font-s"])</script><script>self.__next_f.push([1,"emibold mt-rem32px mb-rem16px break-words print:mt-rem12px print:text-rem19px print:leading-rem27px print:font-semibold print:mb-rem8px  \",\"children\":[\"How can you prevent head injuries?\"]}],[\"$\",\"p\",\"6ee74c283a30\",{\"data-identity\":\"paragraph-element\",\"className\":\"text-gray-800 my-rem16px text-rem19px leading-rem34px print:text-rem15px print:leading-rem20px print:font-normal print:my-rem8px  \",\"children\":[\"Head injuries often happen suddenly. Because you can’t plan for them, you may not always be able to prevent one. These general safety tips may reduce your risk:\"]}],[\"$\",\"ul\",\"e7c19bf3a314-parent\",{\"data-identity\":\"unordered-list\",\"className\":\"my-rem16px mx-0 pl-[1.25rem] list-disc marker:text-brandBlue-500 print:marker:text-black marker:pl-rem24px print:my-rem8px print:text-rem15px print:leading-rem20px print:font-normal  \",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"li\",\"e7c19bf3a314\",{\"className\":\"mb-rem12px pl-rem12px text-gray-800 print:mb-rem4px text-rem19px leading-rem34px print:text-rem15px print:leading-rem20px print:font-normal \",\"children\":[\"Wear the right protective equipment for all activities and sports, especially helmets or protective headwear.\"]}],[\"$\",\"li\",\"55eaf0a41318\",{\"className\":\"mb-rem12px pl-rem12px text-gray-800 print:mb-rem4px text-rem19px leading-rem34px print:text-rem15px print:leading-rem20px print:font-normal \",\"children\":[\"Always wear your seatbelt.\"]}],[\"$\",\"li\",\"0e6619a05f03\",{\"className\":\"mb-rem12px pl-rem12px text-gray-800 print:mb-rem4px text-rem19px leading-rem34px print:text-rem15px print:leading-rem20px print:font-normal \",\"children\":[\"Make sure your home and workspace are free of clutter that could trip you or others.\"]}],[\"$\",\"li\",\"32f8a4dfe2a2\",{\"className\":\"mb-rem12px pl-rem12px text-gray-800 print:mb-rem4px text-rem19px leading-rem34px print:text-rem15px print:leading-rem20px print:font-normal \",\"children\":[\"Always use the proper tools or equipment at home to reach things. Never stand on chairs, tables or countertops.\"]}]]}]]}]]}],false]}]\n59:[\"$\",\"div\",\"31314a675f95f2d18f74b740ea624743\",{\"children\":[[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"data-identity\":\"article-section\",\"id\":\"living-with\",\"className\":\"scroll-mt-[112px]\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"h2\",null,{\"data-identity\":\"headline\",\"id\":\"$undefined\",\"className\":\"text-gray-900 font-bold leading-rem34px text-rem32px bp600:text-rem40px bp600:leading-rem44px print:text-rem22px print:leading-rem31px print:font-bold mt-rem56px print:mt-rem24px mb-rem16px print:mb-rem8px print:text-rem22px print:leading-rem31px print:font-bold break-words\",\"children\":\"Living With\"}],\"$undefined\",[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"data-identity\":\"rich-text\",\"className\":\" after:content-[''] after:table\",\"id\":\"$undefined\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"h3\",\"eb24fc56824e\",{\"data-identity\":\"headline\",\"id\":\"$undefined\",\"className\":\"text-gray-900 font-bold leading-rem30px text-rem25px bp600:text-rem32px bp600:leading-rem38px print:text-rem19px print:leading-rem27px print:font-semibold mt-rem32px mb-rem16px break-words print:mt-rem12px print:text-rem19px print:leading-rem27px print:font-semibold print:mb-rem8px  \",\"children\":[\"How do I know if my head injury is serious?\"]}],[\"$\",\"p\",\"d6edafef3c06\",{\"data-identity\":\"paragraph-element\",\"className\":\"text-gray-800 my-rem16px text-rem19px leading-rem34px print:text-rem15px print:leading-rem20px print:font-normal print:my-rem8px  \",\"children\":[\"All head injuries are serious because it’s impossible for you to know if an injury damages your brain or the \",[\"$\",\"a\",\"baee91c0c69c1\",{\"data-identity\":\"link\",\"href\":\"https://my.clevelandclinic.org/health/body/21640-blood-vessels\",\"target\":\"_blank\",\"className\":\"text-brandBlue-500 print:text-black underline underline-offset-[5px] print:no-underline decoration-1 break-words hover:text-blue-800 transition\",\"children\":[\"blood vessels\"]}],\" around it. Visit a healthcare provider or go to the emergency room if you’ve experienced a head injury and notice any symptoms, even if they don’t start right away. Only a healthcare provider can diagnose a head injury properly and make sure your brain isn’t affected.\"]}],[\"$\",\"h3\",\"30c05a0550b2\",{\"data-identity"])</script><script>self.__next_f.push([1,"\":\"headline\",\"id\":\"$undefined\",\"className\":\"text-gray-900 font-bold leading-rem30px text-rem25px bp600:text-rem32px bp600:leading-rem38px print:text-rem19px print:leading-rem27px print:font-semibold mt-rem32px mb-rem16px break-words print:mt-rem12px print:text-rem19px print:leading-rem27px print:font-semibold print:mb-rem8px  \",\"children\":[\"Which questions should I ask my doctor?\"]}],[\"$\",\"p\",\"3dcd9a28d970\",{\"data-identity\":\"paragraph-element\",\"className\":\"text-gray-800 my-rem16px text-rem19px leading-rem34px print:text-rem15px print:leading-rem20px print:font-normal print:my-rem8px  \",\"children\":[\"You may want to ask your provider:\"]}],[\"$\",\"ul\",\"a074f4421612-parent\",{\"data-identity\":\"unordered-list\",\"className\":\"my-rem16px mx-0 pl-[1.25rem] list-disc marker:text-brandBlue-500 print:marker:text-black marker:pl-rem24px print:my-rem8px print:text-rem15px print:leading-rem20px print:font-normal  \",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"li\",\"a074f4421612\",{\"className\":\"mb-rem12px pl-rem12px text-gray-800 print:mb-rem4px text-rem19px leading-rem34px print:text-rem15px print:leading-rem20px print:font-normal \",\"children\":[\"Which type of head injury do I have?\"]}],[\"$\",\"li\",\"3391936eaded\",{\"className\":\"mb-rem12px pl-rem12px text-gray-800 print:mb-rem4px text-rem19px leading-rem34px print:text-rem15px print:leading-rem20px print:font-normal \",\"children\":[\"Which tests will I need?\"]}],[\"$\",\"li\",\"f5d46e72ff8f\",{\"className\":\"mb-rem12px pl-rem12px text-gray-800 print:mb-rem4px text-rem19px leading-rem34px print:text-rem15px print:leading-rem20px print:font-normal \",\"children\":[\"Will I need surgery?\"]}],\"$L87\",\"$L88\"]}]]}]]}],false]}]\n5a:[\"$\",\"div\",\"53acedff5228f0290f7467095147b92e\",{\"children\":[[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"data-identity\":\"article-section\",\"id\":\"additional-common-questions\",\"className\":\"scroll-mt-[112px]\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"h2\",null,{\"data-identity\":\"headline\",\"id\":\"$undefined\",\"className\":\"text-gray-900 font-bold leading-rem34px text-rem32px bp600:text-rem40px bp600:leading-rem44px print:text-rem22px print:leading-rem31px print:font-bold mt-rem56px print:mt-rem24px mb-rem16px print:mb-rem8px print:text-rem22px print:leading-rem31px print:font-bold break-words\",\"children\":\"Additional Common Questions\"}],\"$undefined\",[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"data-identity\":\"rich-text\",\"className\":\" after:content-[''] after:table\",\"id\":\"$undefined\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"h3\",\"ad8d4af132cc\",{\"data-identity\":\"headline\",\"id\":\"$undefined\",\"className\":\"text-gray-900 font-bold leading-rem30px text-rem25px bp600:text-rem32px bp600:leading-rem38px print:text-rem19px print:leading-rem27px print:font-semibold mt-rem32px mb-rem16px break-words print:mt-rem12px print:text-rem19px print:leading-rem27px print:font-semibold print:mb-rem8px  \",\"children\":[\"Can you die from a head injury years later?\"]}],[\"$\",\"p\",\"6038350c3c99\",{\"data-identity\":\"paragraph-element\",\"className\":\"text-gray-800 my-rem16px text-rem19px leading-rem34px print:text-rem15px print:leading-rem20px print:font-normal print:my-rem8px  \",\"children\":[\"Yes, it’s possible for a head injury to be fatal or contribute to a person dying, even years after the fact. This usually happens in people who experience multiple, repeated head injuries (especially concussions or other types of traumatic brain injuries).\"]}],[\"$\",\"p\",\"56ea27d755ad\",{\"data-identity\":\"paragraph-element\",\"className\":\"text-gray-800 my-rem16px text-rem19px leading-rem34px print:text-rem15px print:leading-rem20px print:font-normal print:my-rem8px  \",\"children\":[\"Experiencing multiple head injuries increases your risk of \",[\"$\",\"a\",\"c20b5c238a7a1\",{\"data-identity\":\"link\",\"href\":\"https://my.clevelandclinic.org/health/diseases/17686-chronic-traumatic-encephalopathy-cte\",\"target\":\"_blank\",\"className\":\"text-brandBlue-500 print:text-black underline underline-offset-[5px] print:no-underline decoration-1 break-words hover:text-blue-800 transition\",\"children\":[\"chronic traumatic encephalopathy (CTE)\"]}],\". CTE affects how areas of your brain function, communicate and work with each other.\"]}]]}]]}],false]}]\n5b:[[\"$\",\"h3\",null,{\"data-identity\":\"headline\",\"id\":\"$undefined\",\"cl"])</script><script>self.__next_f.push([1,"assName\":\"text-gray-900 font-bold leading-rem30px text-rem25px bp600:text-rem32px bp600:leading-rem38px print:text-rem19px print:leading-rem27px print:font-semibold mt-rem32px mb-rem16px print:mt-rem12px print:mb-rem8px print:text-rem19px print:leading-rem27px print:font-semibold\",\"children\":\"A note from Cleveland Clinic\"}],[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"data-identity\":\"rich-text\",\"className\":\" after:content-[''] after:table\",\"id\":\"$undefined\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"p\",\"77724019b5dc\",{\"data-identity\":\"paragraph-element\",\"className\":\"text-gray-800 my-rem16px text-rem19px leading-rem34px print:text-rem15px print:leading-rem20px print:font-normal print:my-rem8px  \",\"children\":[\"Head injuries can include everything from a light bonk on the head to a life-threatening emergency. Even if everyday bumps and knocks don’t usually need special treatment, don’t ignore pain, swelling or other symptoms you notice.\"]}],[\"$\",\"p\",\"181c2c21406c\",{\"data-identity\":\"paragraph-element\",\"className\":\"text-gray-800 my-rem16px text-rem19px leading-rem34px print:text-rem15px print:leading-rem20px print:font-normal print:my-rem8px  \",\"children\":[\"Sometimes, potentially severe complications start small and get worse over time. You don’t need to panic, but don’t take a chance with your head and brain health. Going to the ER is your best bet when you notice symptoms or changes.\"]}]]}]]\n5c:[[\"$\",\"$L89\",\"0\",{\"title\":\"Better health starts here\",\"blurb\":\"Sign up for our Health Essentials emails for expert guidance on nutrition, fitness, sleep, skin care and more.\",\"cadence\":null,\"iconImage\":\"https://assets.clevelandclinic.org/transform/482db8cd-aa1e-45b5-a2a4-cf6aa5e5d2d4/Health-Essentials\",\"secondaryLogo\":{\"alt\":\"Health Essentials logo\",\"width\":200,\"height\":40,\"linkHref\":\"https://health.clevelandclinic.org/\",\"sizes\":\"150px, (min-width: 600px) 200px\",\"className\":\"w-[150px] h-[30px] bp600:w-[200px] bp600:h-[40px]\",\"logoType\":\"health-essentials\"},\"buttonText\":\" Sign up\",\"buttonUrl\":\"https://my.clevelandclinic.org/health-essentials-sign-up\",\"buttonNewTab\":false,\"exampleEmailLink\":