erline-offset-[5px] print:no-underline decoration-1 break-words hover:text-blue-800 transition\",\"children\":[\"blurry vision\"]}],\" or \",[\"$\",\"a\",\"07782fa7a8999\",{\"data-identity\":\"link\",\"href\":\"https://my.clevelandclinic.org/health/diseases/22422-anisocoria\",\"target\":\"_blank\",\"className\":\"text-brandBlue-500 print:text-black underline underline-offset-[5px] print:no-underline decoration-1 break-words hover:text-blue-800 transition\",\"children\":[\"anisocoria\"]}],\").\"]}]\n68:[\"$\",\"li\",\"1b3f44920d38\",{\"className\":\"mb-rem12px pl-rem12px text-gray-800 print:mb-rem4px text-rem19px leading-rem34px print:text-rem15px print:leading-rem20px print:font-normal \",\"children\":[\"Losing consciousness (passing out or \",[\"$\",\"a\",\"5bd206cbe5d91\",{\"data-identity\":\"link\",\"href\":\"https://my.clevelandclinic.org/health/symptoms/21699-fainting\",\"target\":\"_blank\",\"className\":\"text-brandBlue-500 print:text-black underline underline-offset-[5px] print:no-underline decoration-1 break-words hover:text-blue-800 transition\",\"children\":[\"fainting\"]}],\").\"]}]\n69:[\"$\",\"li\",\"5be80414adc9\",{\"className\":\"mb-rem12px pl-rem12px text-gray-800 print:mb-rem4px text-rem19px leading-rem34px print:text-rem15px print:leading-rem20px print:font-normal \",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"a\",\"cd71e43c4ff80\",{\"data-identity\":\"link\",\"href\":\"https://my.clevelandclinic.org/health/diseases/22789-seizure\",\"target\":\"_blank\",\"className\":\"text-brandBlue-500 print:text-black underline underline-offset-[5px] print:no-underline decoration-1 break-words hover:text-blue-800 transition\",\"children\":[\"Seizures\"]}],\".\"]}]\n6a:[\"$\",\"h4\",\"dfbc7feb299a\",{\"data-identity\":\"headline\",\"id\":\"$undefined\",\"className\":\"text-gray-900 font-bold leading-rem24px text-rem20px bp600:text-rem25px bp600:leading-rem30px print:text-rem15px print:leading-rem20px print:font-bold mt-rem32px mb-rem16px break-words print:mt-rem12px print:text-rem19px print:leading-rem27px print:font-semibold print:mb-rem8px  \",\"children\":[\"How long after a head injury can symptoms occur?\"]}]\n6b:[\"$\",\"p\",\"186131516b2e\",{\"data-identity\":\"paragraph-element\",\"className\":\"text-gray-800 my-rem16px text-rem19px leading-rem34px print:text-rem15px print:leading-rem20px print:font-normal print:my-rem8px  \",\"children\":[\"Many head injuries don’t cause symptoms right away, especially closed head injuries that may be harder to notice at first. It can take hours, days or even weeks to start noticing signs or symptoms.\"]}]\n6c:[\"$\",\"p\",\"b446d288d724\",{\"data-identity\":\"paragraph-element\",\"className\":\"text-gray-800 my-rem16px text-rem19px leading-rem34px print:text-rem15px print:leading-rem20px print:font-normal print:my-rem8px  \",\"children\":[\"Visit a healthcare provider or go to the emergency room if you know you experienced a head injury or trauma and start experiencing symptoms of a head injury, even if you don’t notice them right away.\"]}]\n6d:[\"$\",\"h3\",\"9e765b4cd177\",{\"data-identity\":\"headline\",\"id\":\"$undefined\",\"className\":\"text-gray-900 font-bold leading-rem30px text-rem25px bp600:text-rem32px bp600:leading-rem38px print:text-rem19px print:leading-rem27px print:font-semibold mt-rem32px mb-rem16px break-words print:mt-rem12px print:text-rem19px print:leading-rem27px print:font-semibold print:mb-rem8px  \",\"children\":[\"What are complications of head injuries?\"]}]\n6e:[\"$\",\"p\",\"1fdf48e309"])</script><script>self.__next_f.push([1,"b9\",{\"data-identity\":\"paragraph-element\",\"className\":\"text-gray-800 my-rem16px text-rem19px leading-rem34px print:text-rem15px print:leading-rem20px print:font-normal print:my-rem8px  \",\"children\":[\"Bleeding inside your skull (a \",[\"$\",\"a\",\"41425a4c88721\",{\"data-identity\":\"link\",\"href\":\"https://my.clevelandclinic.org/health/diseases/21183-subdural-hematoma\",\"target\":\"_blank\",\"className\":\"text-brandBlue-500 print:text-black underline underline-offset-[5px] print:no-underline decoration-1 break-words hover:text-blue-800 transition\",\"children\":[\"subdural hematoma\"]}],\") is a potentially severe complication of a head injury. If blood builds up inside your skull, it can put extra pressure on your brain and damage it.\"]}]\n6f:[\"$\",\"p\",\"8a07c1b1c56d\",{\"data-identity\":\"paragraph-element\",\"className\":\"text-gray-800 my-rem16px text-rem19px leading-rem34px print:text-rem15px print:leading-rem20px print:font-normal print:my-rem8px  \",\"children\":[\"Head injuries may also cause \",[\"$\",\"a\",\"a65ae25074471\",{\"data-identity\":\"link\",\"href\":\"https://my.clevelandclinic.org/health/diseases/14480-brain-bleed-hemorrhage-intracranial-hemorrhage\",\"target\":\"_blank\",\"className\":\"text-brandBlue-500 print:text-black underline underline-offset-[5px] print:no-underline decoration-1 break-words hover:text-blue-800 transition\",\"children\":[\"intracranial hemorrhage\"]}],\" — a type of \",[\"$\",\"a\",\"a65ae25074473\",{\"data-identity\":\"link\",\"href\":\"https://my.clevelandclinic.org/health/diseases/5601-stroke\",\"target\":\"_blank\",\"className\":\"text-brandBlue-500 print:text-black underline underline-offset-[5px] print:no-underline decoration-1 break-words hover:text-blue-800 transition\",\"children\":[\"stroke\"]}],\".\"]}]\n70:[\"$\",\"p\",\"ec554e6d58ca\",{\"data-identity\":\"paragraph-element\",\"className\":\"text-gray-800 my-rem16px text-rem19px leading-rem34px print:text-rem15px print:leading-rem20px print:font-normal print:my-rem8px  \",\"children\":[\"These complications can cause short-term or permanent damage to your brain.\"]}]\n71:[\"$\",\"div\",\"ec554e6d58ca_mobile_ad\",{\"data-identity\":\"billboard-ad\",\"className\":\"flex bp1100:hidden print:hidden max-w-[400px] min-w-[300px] m-auto items-center justify-center bg-gray-300 pt-rem16px pb-[3.125rem] my-rem32px  \",\"children\":[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"max-w-[300px] mx-auto\",\"children\":[null,[\"$\",\"p\",null,{\"className\":\"text-gray-800 uppercase text-rem10px leading-rem16px mx-auto w-fit\",\"children\":\"Advertisement\"}],[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"flex bp1100:hidden flex-col items-center justify-center\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"data-identity\":\"ad-slot\",\"id\":\"billboard6_300x250_mobile\",\"className\":\"ad-reset w-[300px] !min-h-[250px] flex bg-gray-300\"}],null]}]]}]}]\n72:[\"$\",\"p\",\"e4ae97ec4a34\",{\"data-identity\":\"paragraph-element\",\"className\":\"text-gray-800 my-rem16px text-rem19px leading-rem34px print:text-rem15px print:leading-rem20px print:font-normal print:my-rem8px  \",\"children\":[\"Some people with mild head injuries have short-term memory loss and may not remember the hit or injury that caused the damage. More severe head injuries can permanently affect your brain function. You might experience permanent memory issues, mental health conditions or lose some of your ability to move or use parts of your body.\"]}]\n73:[\"$\",\"p\",\"71e060089880\",{\"data-identity\":\"paragraph-element\",\"className\":\"text-gray-800 my-rem16px text-rem19px leading-rem34px print:text-rem15px print:leading-rem20px print:font-normal print:my-rem8px  \",\"children\":[\"Head injuries can be fatal if they damage your brain’s ability to control your \",[\"$\",\"a\",\"263b67def9e41\",{\"data-identity\":\"link\",\"href\":\"https://my.clevelandclinic.org/health/body/21704-heart\",\"target\":\"_blank\",\"className\":\"text-brandBlue-500 print:text-black underline underline-offset-[5px] print:no-underline decoration-1 break-words hover:text-blue-800 transition\",\"children\":[\"heart\"]}],\", \",[\"$\",\"a\",\"263b67def9e43\",{\"data-identity\":\"link\",\"href\":\"https://my.clevelandclinic.org/health/body/8960-lungs\",\"target\":\"_blank\",\"className\":\"text-brandBlue-500 print:text-black underline underline-offset-[5px] print:no-underl"])</script><script>self.__next_f.push([1,"ine decoration-1 break-words hover:text-blue-800 transition\",\"children\":[\"lungs\"]}],\" or other vital systems that keep you alive.\"]}]\n74:[\"$\",\"h3\",\"90606c775c9a\",{\"data-identity\":\"headline\",\"id\":\"$undefined\",\"className\":\"text-gray-900 font-bold leading-rem30px text-rem25px bp600:text-rem32px bp600:leading-rem38px print:text-rem19px print:leading-rem27px print:font-semibold mt-rem32px mb-rem16px break-words print:mt-rem12px print:text-rem19px print:leading-rem27px print:font-semibold print:mb-rem8px  \",\"children\":[\"What causes head injuries?\"]}]\n75:[\"$\",\"p\",\"2da00f0faa97\",{\"data-identity\":\"paragraph-element\",\"className\":\"text-gray-800 my-rem16px text-rem19px leading-rem34px print:text-rem15px print:leading-rem20px print:font-normal print:my-rem8px  \",\"children\":[\"Any strong force or impact can cause a head injury. You might picture something hitting you in the head, or smacking your head off an object (and those are common causes). But it’s also possible to experience a head injury from any force that suddenly shakes your body hard enough to make your head move violently.\"]}]\n76:[\"$\",\"p\",\"f68eca7fee39\",{\"data-identity\":\"paragraph-element\",\"className\":\"text-gray-800 my-rem16px text-rem19px leading-rem34px print:text-rem15px print:leading-rem20px print:font-normal print:my-rem8px  \",\"children\":[\"Some of the most common causes of head injuries include:\"]}]\n77:[\"$\",\"ul\",\"db40e20b8e75-parent\",{\"data-identity\":\"unordered-list\",\"className\":\"my-rem16px mx-0 pl-[1.25rem] list-disc marker:text-brandBlue-500 print:marker:text-black marker:pl-rem24px print:my-rem8px print:text-rem15px print:leading-rem20px print:font-normal  \",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"li\",\"db40e20b8e75\",{\"className\":\"mb-rem12px pl-rem12px text-gray-800 print:mb-rem4px text-rem19px leading-rem34px print:text-rem15px print:leading-rem20px print:font-normal \",\"children\":[\"Falls.\"]}],[\"$\",\"li\",\"f9feeb0a0f3b\",{\"className\":\"mb-rem12px pl-rem12px t